## Introduction to C# <a name="introduction"></a>

### What is C#?
C# is a modern, object-oriented programming language developed by Microsoft. It's part of the .NET ecosystem and combines the power of C++ with the simplicity of Java.

### Key Characteristics
- **Object-Oriented**: Classes, inheritance, polymorphism
- **Type-Safe**: Compile-time type checking
- **Garbage Collected**: Automatic memory management
- **Modern**: LINQ, async/await, nullable reference types
- **Versatile**: Web, desktop, mobile, game development
- **Performance**: Fast execution on .NET runtime

### History & Evolution
```
C# 1.0 (2002): Basic OOP, generics foundation
C# 2.0 (2005): Generics, nullable types
C# 3.0 (2007): LINQ, lambda expressions
C# 4.0 (2010): Dynamic typing, named parameters
C# 5.0 (2012): Async/await
C# 6.0 (2015): String interpolation, null-conditional
C# 7.0 (2017): Tuples, pattern matching
C# 8.0 (2019): Nullable reference types, records
C# 9.0 (2020): Init-only properties, records enhancement
C# 10.0 (2021): Record structs, file-scoped types
C# 11.0 (2022): Generic attributes, required members
C# 12.0 (2023): Primary constructors, collection literals
```

### Use Cases
- Web Applications (ASP.NET Core)
- Desktop Applications (WinForms, WPF)
- Game Development (Unity)
- Mobile Apps (Xamarin, MAUI)
- Console Applications
- Cloud Services (Azure)
- Microservices

