## Async/Await & Multithreading <a name="async"></a>

### 1. Async/Await

```csharp
// Synchronous (blocking)
public string FetchData()
{
    using var client = new HttpClient();
    var response = client.GetStringAsync("https://api.example.com/data").Result;
    return response; // Blocks until complete
}

// Asynchronous (non-blocking)
public async Task<string> FetchDataAsync()
{
    using var client = new HttpClient();
    var response = await client.GetStringAsync("https://api.example.com/data");
    return response; // Returns immediately, continues when ready
}

// Usage
async Task Main()
{
    string data = await FetchDataAsync();
    Console.WriteLine(data);
}

// Multiple async operations
async Task<(string, int)> FetchMultipleAsync()
{
    var task1 = FetchDataAsync();
    var task2 = FetchCountAsync();
    
    // Wait for both
    await Task.WhenAll(task1, task2);
    
    return (await task1, await task2);
}
```

### 2. Task & Async Methods

```csharp
// Returns Task (no result)
public async Task ProcessDataAsync()
{
    await Task.Delay(1000); // Simulate work
    Console.WriteLine("Done");
