### Q2: Explain the difference between value types and reference types.

**Answer:**
- **Value Types** (stored on stack): int, float, bool, char, struct, enum
  - Copied when assigned
  - Passed by value by default
  - Faster access
  
- **Reference Types** (stored on heap): class, string, array, interface, delegate
  - Reference is copied, not data
  - Passed by reference by default
  - Requires garbage collection

**Example:**
```csharp
int a = 10;        // Value type
int b = a;         // Copy
b = 20;
Console.WriteLine(a); // Still 10

Person p1 = new Person { Name = "John" };
Person p2 = p1;    // Reference copy
p2.Name = "Jane";
Console.WriteLine(p1.Name); // "Jane" (changed!)
```

